<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sisak</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Siscia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sisak is a town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> at the confluence of the Kupa and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a>, on the site of Roman Siscia, an important city and mint of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>. In the 9th century it was the seat of the dukes of Pannonian Croatia. In 1593 a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> and Croatian army defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at the Battle of Sisak, a turning point in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-habsburg-wars">Ottoman–Habsburg wars</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sisak.jpg" alt="Sisak" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Donatus (Darko Tepert) · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sisak_Veliki_Kaptol.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
